@startuml
!theme materia

<style>
document {
  BackgroundColor transparent
  `materia wants Verdana, which isn't installed
  FontName sans-serif
}
</style>

title
  =Sending data with a token
  ==The sender obtains its own token from the identity provider
end title

participant "Sending system" as client
participant "Identity provider" as idp
participant "Stroom-Proxy\nor Stroom" as stroom

== Obtaining a token ==

client -> idp: POST //token endpoint//\ngrant_type=client_credentials\nclient_id, client secret, scope
idp --> client: access_token, expires_in
note right of client
  The scope must be one that yields
  a token for Stroom. A token minted
  for another application will not
  validate here
end note

== Sending data ==

client -> stroom: POST /datafeed\nAuthorization: Bearer <access_token>\nFeed, System and Environment headers
stroom -> idp: GET //jwks_uri// (cached)
idp --> stroom: Signing keys
stroom -> stroom: Verify signature, issuer,\naudience and expiry.\nRecord uniqueIdentityClaim\nagainst the received data
stroom --> client: 200

== When the token expires ==

client -> stroom: POST /datafeed (expired token)
stroom --> client: 401
client -> idp: Request a new token
idp --> client: A fresh access_token

@enduml
